Vendored PuTTY terminal emulator
================================

This directory contains a subset of the PuTTY source distribution, used by
QEMU-mod's native Win32 UI to provide a real VT100/VT220/xterm terminal
emulator for serial ports and the HMP monitor, in place of QEMU's own
minimal ui/vt100.c.

Upstream
--------

    Project:  PuTTY
    Version:  0.85
    Source:   https://the.earth.li/~sgtatham/putty/0.85/putty-0.85.tar.gz
    Author:   Simon Tatham and others (see LICENCE)

Licence
-------

PuTTY is distributed under the MIT licence, which is GPL-compatible.  The
full copyright notice and permission text are reproduced verbatim in the
file `LICENCE` in this directory, copied unaltered from the upstream
distribution.  Every source file here keeps its original header comment.

Nothing in this directory is relicensed.  QEMU-mod as a whole remains
GPL-2.0-or-later; the MIT terms of these files permit that combination, and
`LICENCE` is what satisfies MIT's requirement that the copyright notice and
permission notice accompany substantial portions of the software.

What is here, and what was changed
----------------------------------

Everything in this directory is verbatim upstream PuTTY, with exactly two
exceptions, both noted below.

    terminal/terminal.c      the terminal emulator itself
    terminal/terminal.h
    terminal/bidi.c          bidirectional text and Arabic shaping
    terminal/bidi.h
    terminal/lineedit.c      the terminal-side line editor
    callback.c               PuTTY's toplevel-callback queue
    timing.c                 PuTTY's timer wheel
    utils/                   the general-purpose utilities the above need
                             (memory, strings, tree234, bufchain, marshal,
                             UTF-8, wcwidth, and the Conf container)
    windows/unicode.c        Windows codepage and line-drawing tables
    windows/blink_time.c     GetCaretBlinkTime() wrapper
    windows/filename.c       Filename, needed by Conf
    windows/fontspec.c       FontSpec, needed by Conf
    unicode/*.h              generated Unicode character property tables
    *.h                      PuTTY's headers, unmodified; platform.h is
                             upstream's windows/platform.h and help.h is
                             upstream's windows/help.h

The two files that are NOT upstream:

    cmake.h                  written for QEMU-mod.  Upstream generates this
                             from cmake/cmake.h.in using CMake feature
                             probes; we do not run PuTTY's build system, so
                             the handful of macros the vendored subset
                             actually tests are hardcoded for
                             x86_64-w64-mingw32.  Marked SPDX MIT to match
                             the code it configures.

    README.qemu-mod          this file.

No upstream .c or .h file in this directory has been edited.  The pieces of
PuTTY that we do *not* vendor -- its line discipline, session logging,
printing and configuration loading -- are replaced by original QEMU-mod code
in ../win32-term-shim.c, which is GPL-2.0-or-later and not part of PuTTY.

Updating
--------

Re-copy the file list above from a newer PuTTY tarball, re-run the build,
and fix up ../win32-term.c (the TermWin implementation) against any change
to `struct TermWinVtable` in putty.h.  Do not reformat or restyle anything
here: QEMU's checkpatch.pl will reject these files, and that is correct.
